    <briefdescription>
<para>Primary namespace for the µTest++ testing framework. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>The <computeroutput><ref refid="namespacemicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus" kindref="compound">micro_os_plus::micro_test_plus</ref></computeroutput> namespace encapsulates all core components, types, and utilities of the µTest++ testing framework, providing a dedicated scope for its public API.</para>
<para>The main classes (the runners, and the suites and test cases) are defined directly in this namespace. Several nested namespaces group specific aspects of the framework: <computeroutput>math</computeroutput> (mathematical utilities), <computeroutput><ref refid="namespacemicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1extension" kindref="compound">extension</ref></computeroutput> (the concepts for custom comparators, operators, and helpers), <computeroutput><ref refid="namespacemicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1reflection" kindref="compound">reflection</ref></computeroutput> (source locations and type names), <computeroutput><ref refid="namespacemicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1literals" kindref="compound">literals</ref></computeroutput> (user-defined literals), <computeroutput><ref refid="namespacemicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1operators" kindref="compound">operators</ref></computeroutput> (comparison and logical operators), <computeroutput><ref refid="namespacemicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1utility" kindref="compound">utility</ref></computeroutput> (utility functions), and <computeroutput><ref refid="namespacemicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1detail" kindref="compound">detail</ref></computeroutput> (internal implementation details, including the reporters and the value wrappers).</para>
<para>By grouping all definitions within this namespace and its sub-namespaces, the framework achieves clear code organisation, minimises naming conflicts, and enhances maintainability.</para>
<para>All public API definitions are implemented in the <computeroutput>include/micro-os-plus/micro-test-plus</computeroutput> folder, ensuring a clear separation from user code and facilitating straightforward integration with the wider µOS++ ecosystem. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
